# Club & Grub - World 3, stage 1 (second half) in co-op: "Blizzard Pass" for two (designer DB2; DESIGN.md D.9).
# The co-op file of levels/w3_l1b.lvl (kind = coop, coop_of, coop_base_hash; never edit the solo file). The gusts
# are the solo ones. Main-path gate (a sub-stage needs one), with its x2 tablet:
#  - 'hut': the plateau before the hut is a crust over a keeper hall 4 rows high, two Shellback turtles inside and
#    an ice door at its end (the foot of a rock spire nobody climbs). A Shellback turns its front to the nearer
#    hero every tick, so one hero baits it while the other drops through a hole in the crust behind it; a vine in
#    the first hole is the way back up for the second pincer. The hut and the exit lie in the hollow behind the door.
# x2 secret 'lee': a ledge 8 rows over the shelter ridge, a Shoulder Hop up (painting 25); the solo file's two
# ridge chargers beside it are left out (a sleeping one would be a lone hero's springboard onto it). The ridge walker
# is a Shellback. The lee works everywhere (a crouching hero shelters his partner behind him from the gust - a sign
# at the crevasse tells it), but it is no gate (G55): the first hero over a gap has no lee, so he crosses in a lull,
# and so could a lone hero.
# Not built: the Snatcher pterodactyls (no gust-riding Snatcher exists).

